{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Braiding.TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Braiding.TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RpowAlgebra","lean:module:QOU.Braiding.HnMarkovTrace"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.trMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.trMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm_canonical","kind":"instance","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm.lean#L99-L112","doc":"Canonical concrete instance of `TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm q` for `q > 1`.\n\nThe instance uses the same closed-form expression as the canonical\n`MarkovTraceTower` instance (HnMarkovTrace.lean): the value at every\n`n ≥ 2` is `(q^{5/2} - q^{1/2} + q² + q) / (q² + q)`. The `closed_form`\nfield is satisfied by `rfl`. This discharges the class abstraction with\na concrete witness whose Markov-invariance is proved via\n`trm_hopf_sigma1_sq_markov_invariant`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.trm_hopf_sigma1_sq_markov_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.trm_hopf_sigma1_sq_markov_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm.lean#L87-L97","doc":"Markov-invariance of tr_M(σ_1²) across H_n for n ≥ 2.\nFollows from the Markov axiom tr_M(α · σ_n^{±1}) = z^{±1} tr_M(α)\nwhen α and σ_n are disjoint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.trm_hopf_sigma1_sq_closed_form_simplified","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.trm_hopf_sigma1_sq_closed_form_simplified","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm.lean#L55-L85","doc":"The closed form equals the simplified form 1 + (q − 1) · q^{−1/2}.\n\nProof strategy: substitute u := sqrt(q) > 0 and reduce to the\npolynomial-in-u identity\n    (u^5 - u + u^4 + u^2) / (u^4 + u^2) = 1 + (u^2 - 1) · u⁻¹\nwhich closes via `field_simp + ring` under `u > 0`.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm.closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm.closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The closed form: tr_M(σ_1²) = (q^{5/2} − q^{1/2} + q² + q) / (q² + q). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm.trM_sigma1_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm.trM_sigma1_sq","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Canonical-Markov-trace value of σ_1² in H_n(q) at any n ≥ 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Hypothesis: q is in the Wenzl positivity regime (q > 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm","kind":"class","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/TrMHopfSigma1SqClosedForm.lean#L33-L53","doc":"Closed-form value of the canonical Markov trace of σ_1² in H_n(q),\nexpressed as a real-valued function of q > 1.\n\nThe propositional content is the algebraic identity\n    (q^{5/2} − q^{1/2} + q² + q) / (q² + q) = 1 + (q − 1) · q^{−1/2}\nthat the Markov-trace value satisfies for every n ≥ 2.\nMarkov-invariance under stabilisation is captured by the\n`MarkovTraceTower` class.\n\n`closed_form` carries the value; `closed_form_equals_simplified`\nfollows from the rpow algebra.\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:trm-hopf-sigma1-sq-closed-form","label":"prop:trm-hopf-sigma1-sq-closed-form","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/trm-hopf-sigma1-sq-closed-form.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}